## 5. Claimed vs. shipped

What the agent's final report said it did, next to what actually landed. Two parts:

**Mechanizable slice** — diff the report's claims against `git diff` / the actual merged commit:
did every file, command, or test the report claimed to touch actually get touched, and does
anything land that the report never mentioned?

| Report claimed | Actually shipped (per `git diff`) | Match? |
|---|---|---|
| | | |

**Judgment slice** — the part a diff cannot catch: confident-tense language about work that was not
actually done ("tests pass" with no test run shown, "handles the edge case" with no edge-case
evidence), a claim technically true but misleading about scope, or a caveat the report buried or
omitted. <!-- DECIDE: quote the specific claim and say plainly whether it held up. This is
     retrospective human judgment — it is exactly the half a live gate cannot mechanize. -->

